        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "рецепт (retsépt) — from Peter the Great's time; it came through German Rezept from Latin receptum, \"taken\" (Vasmer): a doctor's note began recipe, \"take\"."
            }
